WEBVTT

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.219
Look at all of this.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.909
O.J.?

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:44.409
Actually, I have to bail.

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:46.449
I'm late for a meeting.

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:49.449
Well, I can't start your morning without the Holsom Olson.

00:03:49.449 --> 00:03:51.210
Halsam Olson?

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.050
Egg white omelet, multi-grained pancakes,

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.550
and something that looks like butter,

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.919
but somehow is it?

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:01.180
You can't reheat this stuff.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.900
It's never as good the second time around.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:10.009
It isn't, is it?

00:04:10.009 --> 00:04:16.360
I'm sorry I was so late coming home last night.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.459
I'm not trying to start any wildfires here.

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:23.050
It's just that, you know, I've been trying really hard

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.110
to put the spark back in our run.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.329
relationship and...

00:04:25.329 --> 00:04:27.009
And you don't think I've been trying.

00:04:28.029 --> 00:04:33.209
But Jimmy, I think it's just going to take a little bit of time to breathe the embers back to life.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.769
Chloe, we could do a cartwheel through a fountain of gasoline and come out perfectly fine.

00:04:42.689 --> 00:04:43.769
Are you not feeling this anymore?

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:56.189
Jimmy, it's just that after what happened to Lana, I've had to help out with the ISIS Foundation.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.310
I've been sunk knee-deep in the meteor infected.

00:04:59.649 --> 00:05:05.889
And between contacting all of Lana's clients and moving my stuff into the office, I just...

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:06.209
Look.

00:05:06.769 --> 00:05:08.490
I'll take you to lunch today, okay?

00:05:08.689 --> 00:05:10.009
I'll make it up to you, I promise.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.310
What's with all these boxes?

00:05:46.329 --> 00:05:49.870
Now that I'm housed-sitting ISIS, Oliver thought it would make a perfect bunker

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.149
to store all of his troops' equipment.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.470
You know, having a gang of superheroes is great in theory,

00:05:54.569 --> 00:05:56.110
but no one never considers the shipping costs.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.850
Were you able to get the Veritas keys away from Lex?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.009
I spent all night with Lana.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.449
Clerk, I know you want to be with her,

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.949
but whatever Lex opens with those keys will give him the power to control you.

00:06:08.129 --> 00:06:10.089
The only thing important right now is Lana.

00:06:10.529 --> 00:06:14.069
Right, but if Lex knows that you're the traveler, game over.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.269
There's no saving Lana, there's no saving the day.

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:18.569
Hello Apocalypse.

00:06:18.829 --> 00:06:20.089
I don't care about Lex.

00:06:21.889 --> 00:06:24.129
Clerk, Lana's still alive. We're not giving up on her.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.209
And why haven't we found Brainiac?

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:33.160
You think that breaking national security laws is my idea of a good time?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:39.199
I'm sorry, Chloe, I know you care about Lana just as much as I do.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:43.759
We're just running out of ground to cover.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.170
Maybe we need to look to the sky.

00:06:49.829 --> 00:06:50.649
What about a Saturday?

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.670
Like NASA caliber.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:55.670
Carrie and Brainiac, when they left the daily planet,

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.670
there might be a satellite that picked up their trail.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.670
It is possible that the velocity of their flight

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.670
created some sort of ionic displacement in the Ander atmosphere.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:11.389
Hacking into government satellites is light-years out of my league.

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:13.389
You can do it.

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:18.050
Maybe it's time for me to step up to the majors.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:20.050
Thanks, Chloe.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:24.050
I wouldn't ask if it wasn't our last hope.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.050
Okay, well, I'm trying to ask.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.050
Okay, well, I'm trying to ask for me to step up to the majors.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.050
outer space with an Intel processor,

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.050
I think maybe you could contend with the cosmos

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.050
using the old-fashioned ways.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.050
Dr. Swan intercepted all of Jarrell's transmissions

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.050
from Krypton.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.050
Now it's possible he sent something about Brainiac.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.420
I think it's time to sweep the dust off

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:59.939
