00:26:50.299 --> 00:26:54.299
That briefcase is the daily mainframe backup.

00:26:54.299 --> 00:26:58.299
She just happened to lure you to the most useless file on the drive.

00:26:58.299 --> 00:27:00.299
Really?

00:27:00.299 --> 00:27:03.299
You blew it. Now I'm taking over.

00:27:03.299 --> 00:27:04.299
My way.

00:27:04.299 --> 00:27:07.299
Chloe trusted you as much as you seem to trust her.

00:27:07.299 --> 00:27:09.299
She wouldn't get hurt.

00:27:09.299 --> 00:27:12.299
Prison might actually do your relationship some good.

00:27:12.299 --> 00:27:46.079
You're under arrest.

00:27:46.079 --> 00:27:51.789
Chloe'll never talk, you know that?

00:27:51.789 --> 00:27:52.789
I wouldn't worry.

00:27:52.789 --> 00:27:54.789
Agent Weber always leaves a few teeth.

00:27:54.789 --> 00:27:56.789
your teeth.

00:27:56.789 --> 00:28:09.509
Who are you working for?

00:28:09.509 --> 00:28:12.509
I'm not a terrorist, okay?

00:28:12.509 --> 00:28:13.509
I'm one of the good guys.

00:28:13.509 --> 00:28:16.509
Good guys put their country before themselves.

00:28:16.509 --> 00:28:19.509
Who's your network contact?

00:28:19.509 --> 00:28:26.480
I don't have one.

00:28:26.480 --> 00:28:45.319
Why did you access power grids exactly where there just happened to be unexplained energy surges?

00:28:45.319 --> 00:28:49.319
Must be a plan behind it all.

00:28:49.319 --> 00:28:50.319
Did you really think it would all go unnoticed?

00:28:50.319 --> 00:28:53.569
all go unnoticed.

00:28:53.569 --> 00:28:55.569
Don't even think about passing out.

00:28:55.569 --> 00:28:59.490
Give me the taser.

00:28:59.490 --> 00:29:01.490
You really thought you could get away with it all?

00:29:01.490 --> 00:29:03.490
Haven't you figured it out yet?

00:29:03.490 --> 00:29:05.490
I'm not going to tell you anything.

00:29:05.490 --> 00:29:07.490
You need to make a choice right now.

00:29:07.490 --> 00:29:10.490
What's more important?

00:29:10.490 --> 00:29:11.490
The secret?

00:29:11.490 --> 00:29:24.339
or your life?

00:29:24.339 --> 00:29:50.549
Turn this all.

00:29:50.549 --> 00:29:51.549
Is that man enough for you?

00:29:51.549 --> 00:30:01.230
Chloe, hey. It's me.

00:30:01.230 --> 00:30:02.230
Jimmy.

00:30:02.230 --> 00:30:05.230
You're still here.

00:30:05.230 --> 00:30:13.660
I wish you'd let me take you to the hospital.

00:30:13.660 --> 00:30:14.660
let me take you to the hospital.

00:30:14.660 --> 00:30:16.660
I'm fine, really.

00:30:16.660 --> 00:30:18.660
Chloe, you almost die.

00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:20.660
Look, I think I deserve an explanation, preferably the truth this time.

00:30:20.660 --> 00:30:21.660
The truth?

00:30:21.660 --> 00:30:23.660
Why don't you just look at your files?

00:30:23.660 --> 00:30:26.660
Or should I say, my files?

00:30:26.660 --> 00:30:29.660
You stole from me, Jimmy.

00:30:29.660 --> 00:30:31.660
After being coerced by the feds, I mean,

00:30:31.660 --> 00:30:33.660
did you really think that I was a government agent?

00:30:33.660 --> 00:30:36.660
Did you really think I was a terrorist spy?

00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:39.660
Or she didn't give me any choice?

00:30:39.660 --> 00:30:42.660
Besides, what was I supposed to think?

00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:43.660
You were sitting on it?

00:30:43.660 --> 00:30:46.660
enough classified information to start a nuclear war.

00:30:46.660 --> 00:30:48.660
Jimmy, yeah, that was my plan, nuke the whole thing,

00:30:48.660 --> 00:30:50.660
and just start over again.

00:30:50.660 --> 00:30:51.660
Are you kidding me?

00:30:51.660 --> 00:30:55.660
Why didn't you just come to me, like a normal boyfriend?

00:30:55.660 --> 00:30:58.660
Because a normal boyfriend doesn't get lied to

00:30:58.660 --> 00:31:08.309
every five minutes by the girl that he thinks that he's in love with.

00:31:08.309 --> 00:31:09.309
All right, fine, I lied.

00:31:09.309 --> 00:31:13.619
Is that what you want to hear, Jimmy? I'm sorry.

00:31:13.619 --> 00:31:16.619
Is this the point where the sad song comes on and we break up all over again?

00:31:16.619 --> 00:31:20.829
Because I'm not going to make it that easy this time.

00:31:20.829 --> 00:31:27.410
You know what? The Feds are going to find us any moment,

00:31:27.410 --> 00:31:33.410
any moment and then I'll just spend the rest of my life making license plates, so you may as well just fire away.

00:31:33.410 --> 00:31:35.410
Ask me whatever you want.

00:31:35.410 --> 00:32:01.960
You want that more than you want, Clark.

00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:02.960
Oh!

00:32:02.960 --> 00:32:07.960
And by the way, there's no one coming after us. I'm taking care of that.

00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:08.960
How?

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:13.200
You have your secrets and I have mine.

00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:15.200
Deal?

00:32:15.200 --> 00:32:39.670
Mr. Liff, your box.

00:32:39.670 --> 00:35:29.340
Find out who he is and see if he's connected to whatever I'm dealing with in Quebec.

00:35:29.340 --> 00:35:33.599
Beck.

00:35:33.599 --> 00:35:36.389
Busy?

00:35:36.389 --> 00:35:37.389
Mr. Olson.

00:35:37.389 --> 00:35:39.389
I was expecting you.

00:35:39.389 --> 00:35:41.860
I take it.

00:35:41.860 --> 00:35:43.860
Chloe doesn't know how desperate you are.

00:35:43.860 --> 00:35:48.860
I mean, she would never let a friend crawl across burning coals for my help.

00:35:48.860 --> 00:35:55.010
You're Luther, build and burn political ladders for sport.

00:35:55.010 --> 00:36:03.010
What I mean is that, um, you have a poll with these people, and I thought that maybe a string here or a handshake there...

00:36:03.010 --> 00:36:06.219
And stop now.

00:36:06.219 --> 00:36:09.219
I cleared Chloe's name from that suspiciously high-ranking government.

00:36:09.219 --> 00:36:11.219
High-ranking government arrest warrant.

00:36:11.219 --> 00:36:15.219
Special Agent Weber has decided to drop her investigation.

00:36:15.219 --> 00:36:21.019
Thank you.

00:36:21.019 --> 00:36:28.980
There's not that many people eating lunch on Lex Luther's time.

00:36:28.980 --> 00:36:32.949
Why are you helping me?

00:36:32.949 --> 00:36:40.719
You see, Jimmy, in light of recent events,

00:36:40.719 --> 00:36:43.719
I'd like to think of my employees as my new family.

00:36:43.719 --> 00:36:49.110
Families help each other.

00:36:49.110 --> 00:36:51.110
And I know if I ever needed something from you.

00:36:51.110 --> 00:36:54.739
You'd be more than willing to be there for me.

00:36:54.739 --> 00:37:36.179
So Kara's trying to contact you via the fortress from Krypton?

00:37:36.179 --> 00:37:37.179
I know.

00:37:37.179 --> 00:37:38.179
What, Krypton is the planet that exploded, right?

00:37:38.179 --> 00:37:39.179
It sounds.

00:37:39.179 --> 00:37:40.179
Sounds crazy.

00:37:40.179 --> 00:37:42.179
Jerell must have done something to her.

00:37:42.179 --> 00:37:43.179
But Caryl left with Brainiac.

00:37:43.179 --> 00:37:45.179
What does Jarrell have to do with any of this?

00:37:45.179 --> 00:37:47.460
I don't know.

00:37:47.460 --> 00:37:49.460
But how else could her message come through the fortress?

00:37:49.460 --> 00:37:57.150
Clerk, have you considered the possibility that Kara really is on Krypton?

00:37:57.150 --> 00:37:59.150
And it's just a different time zone?

00:37:59.150 --> 00:38:03.429
Like the past.

00:38:03.429 --> 00:38:05.429
You mean like time travel?

00:38:05.429 --> 00:38:07.429
Check this out.

00:38:07.429 --> 00:38:10.429
I followed the trajectory of two blurs that started from the Daily Planet Roof.

00:38:10.429 --> 00:38:13.429
Now, it has to be Kara and Brainiac.

00:38:13.429 --> 00:38:14.429
What is?

00:38:14.429 --> 00:38:17.429
the vortex that they're flying through

00:38:17.429 --> 00:38:20.429
is some kind of intergalactic time portal.

00:38:20.429 --> 00:38:22.429
I mean, look at this.

00:38:22.429 --> 00:38:23.429
Looks like a red star.

00:38:23.429 --> 00:38:26.429
Right, and next to it is a dot, which could be a planet,

00:38:26.429 --> 00:38:28.429
Krypton.

00:38:28.429 --> 00:38:30.429
Now, this picture was taken seconds later.

00:38:30.429 --> 00:38:33.429
The vortex is closed and the red star is gone.

00:38:33.429 --> 00:38:37.219
It's impossible.

00:38:37.219 --> 00:38:40.219
You're saying Kare's actually on Krypton.

00:38:40.219 --> 00:38:43.219
Well, Krypton 1998,

00:38:43.219 --> 00:38:45.219
give or take a few light years.

00:38:45.219 --> 00:38:49.739
That explains.

00:38:49.739 --> 00:38:51.739
How explains how her message mysteriously appeared

00:38:51.739 --> 00:38:52.739
in Swan's journal.

00:38:52.739 --> 00:38:55.739
She sent it to him, hoping that I'd read it.

00:38:55.739 --> 00:38:58.739
Sounds more like a Hail Mary pass.

00:38:58.739 --> 00:39:01.739
Clark, if she sent those messages to Swan and the Fortress,

00:39:01.739 --> 00:39:04.739
that means Kara's desperate to get your attention.

00:39:04.739 --> 00:39:06.739
When I was in the fortress, Carol warned me

00:39:06.739 --> 00:39:08.739
that Brainiac was trying to kill me.

00:39:08.739 --> 00:39:11.739
She must have meant the version of me on Krypton 20 years ago.

00:39:11.739 --> 00:39:14.739
When you were a baby.

00:39:14.739 --> 00:39:16.739
Clark, if you really are in trouble on Krypton,

00:39:16.739 --> 00:39:18.739
you better find a way to get there soon or...

00:39:18.739 --> 00:39:19.739
I'll have never get there soon.

00:39:19.739 --> 00:39:22.309
existed.

00:39:22.309 --> 00:39:25.309
Looks like it's finally time for Kalal to go home.

